        {
          "id": "7ff515ce-6ad6-3076-87b8-e4cffa474e2d",
          "content": {
            "id": "7ff515ce-6ad6-3076-87b8-e4cffa474e2d",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Norway's energy giant Equinor falls into loss",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Norwegian energy giant Equinor said Wednesday it suffered a net loss in the third quarter as it lowered its outlook for oil prices, forcing it to write down the value of its assets.Accounting force companies to regularly restate the value of their assets, and Equinor lowered its forecast of for average crude prices in 2030-2040 to $75 per barrel, thus triggering a write down in the value of some assets.",
